# Real bug found building the E10 kind smoke-test image: with no
# .dockerignore, `docker build` was uploading the live SQLite DB,
# downloaded tool binaries, and test caches into the build context --
# none of which belong in the image, and which (over the slow
# Windows-filesystem-to-WSL2 bridge Docker Desktop uses) turned a
# few-second context transfer into a multi-minute one. See docs/deployment.md.
#
# datasets/ is deliberately NOT excluded (only 32MB -- negligible next to
# the torch/transformers layers already in this image): a second real bug
# found live, this time on the actual Render deployment, was seed.py's
# real-data bootstrap crashing with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named
# 'build_corpus'` because excluding datasets/ here meant corpus.jsonl (and
# every fallback .py builder for it) never existed in ANY Docker-built
# image at all, local kind-cluster or production alike -- not just slower
# to build, genuinely missing. This is the real loghub/EVTX/Zeek/CloudTrail
# data a fresh deployment's seed.py needs to reach local-dev parity.
data/
bin/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
tests/
.git/
